    source_record: NBRC 1020 Se/W solution; complete named stock table and preparation
      notes
    notes: Applies only to NBRC1020 occurrence. NBRC824 has matching two salt amounts
      but no water/preparation denominator; its occurrence is not mapped to this quantified
      stock. Printed formulas are retained literally; omitted hydration is unresolved,
      not an anhydrous assignment. NBRC1020 prints Na2SeO3 4 mg and Na2WO4 4 mg with
      1 L distilled water; the missing hydrate qualifiers do not establish anhydrous
      reagents. JCM317 explicitly prints Na2WO4·2H2O 4 mg with Na2SeO3 4 mg and 1
      L distilled water. The shared nominal amounts and omitted NBRC hydrate do not
      establish either identical or distinct supplied preparations. Retain both source-bound
      partial proposals without merging or co-installing them as proved-distinct owners
      until supplied-form/applicability evidence or an explicitly reviewed common
      nominal scope resolves the overlap. The water amounts are added-water batch
      quantities, not instructions to make up a final litre. Literal printed masses
      and added distilled-water volume per source preparation. G/MG_PER_PREPARATION_WITH_1_L_WATER
      describes a recipe batch containing1L added water, not a final1L solution or
      final concentration.
